# PART 1
H.append('<section class="page">')
H.append('<h1 class="section">Part 1 — The concepts</h1>')
H.append('<span class="badge">For the business owner · no SQL</span>')
H.append('<h2 class="sub">1.1 What RTM does with raw events</h2>')
H.append('<p>Your ACD (Twilio, or any platform) emits low-level events. RTM turns that raw stream into <strong>two clean, business-meaningful models</strong>: a <strong>call lifecycle</strong> and an <strong>agent-status lifecycle</strong> where each status belongs to a <em>status group</em>.</p>')
H.append('<h2 class="sub">1.2 The Twilio gap — and how RTM closes it</h2>')
H.append('<p>Legacy ACDs expose a categorised in-call status (Available → Ringing → Talk → Hold → Wrap → Available). <strong>Twilio does not</strong>: Worker Activity is availability only and does not change during a call. RTM <strong>derives the in-call agent status from the bound call</strong> — Ringing, Talk, Hold, Wrap Up — and writes it into the agent timeline.</p>')
H.append(tbl(["Raw Twilio signal","RTM derived agent status"],[
 ["Reservation created","Ringing"],["Reservation accepted / call assigned","Talk (On Phone)"],
 ["Call held","Hold"],["After-call work","Wrap Up"],["Worker Activity = a break activity","Break"]],"aud-table"))
H.append('<h2 class="sub">1.4 Status groups</h2>')
H.append('<p>Groups: <strong>AVAILABLE, ONPHONE, BREAK, PAPERWORK, TRAINING, SIGNOFF, UNAVAILABLE</strong>. A status listed under a group → that group; any unmapped status falls back to AVAILABLE (if available) else UNAVAILABLE. <strong>SIGNOFF (logged out) is its own group — never folded into UNAVAILABLE.</strong> AHT = Talk + Hold + Wrap Up.</p>')
H.append('<h2 class="sub">1.5 Two roll-up paths to a Business Unit</h2>')
H.append('<ul><li><strong>Calls</strong> roll up by queue: Queue → Business Unit.</li><li><strong>Agent time</strong> rolls up by team: Agent → Agent Group → Super Group → Business Unit.</li></ul>')
H.append('<h2 class="sub">1.6 Why real-time and historical agree</h2>')
H.append('<p>The live grid and the report read the <strong>same persisted, derived states</strong>. With the same status-group rules and units, a historical query reproduces the live numbers.</p>')
